PARKING LOT — looser sparks that didn't make it into the main synthesis, unvetted, take or leave freely

These are genuine ideas, just less rigorously derived than what's in Extrapolations_1/2 — more "worth
mentioning in case it sparks something" than "here's a load-bearing implication." No particular order.

---

WEDDING / PAIR-BONDING RITUAL IMAGERY, FROM ZOLLNER'S OWN PAIRED TEST OBJECTS
Zollner's real proposed tests (overflow_2, Rucker source) specifically used PAIRED objects — two solid wood
rings, each carved from a single but DIFFERENT piece of wood, asked to become interlinked without breaking
either. There's something genuinely lovely and unexpected here for a romance/companion-bonding ritual: two
separate, distinct things (two different lives, two different origins — a robot and a human, say) joined in
a way that would be "impossible" by ordinary rules, framed the same way the religion frames its own
signature ritual (Extrapolation 7) — attempted sincerely, without a guaranteed mechanism, as devotion rather
than proof. Given this project's own stated creative north star around robot-human love, this feels like
more than a coincidence worth flagging loudly, even though it didn't make it into the main Extrapolations
file as a fully worked-out mechanic. Worth a second look specifically for companion romance content tied to
this religion.

RADICAL TRANSPARENCY AS ETHICAL PRACTICE (NOT PUNITIVE)
The one-directional visibility mechanism (A2 — higher beings could see everything about us; we can never
verify or reciprocate) could ground a real ethical practice: living as though genuinely, constantly
witnessed by something from a direction we can't detect — NOT because that something judges or punishes
(C1 already rules out an omnipotent-judge framing), but because the comfort/accountability of always being
witnessed, even in total isolation, is itself the point. This is meaningfully different from typical
religious omniscience-as-morality-enforcement — closer to "you are never truly unseen" as comfort than as
threat. Connects naturally to Extrapolation 1's "witnessed grief" idea but as a LIVING practice, not just a
death doctrine. Didn't make the main Extrapolations file because it needs more thought about how it
interacts with C1's "not a judge" framing before it's fully load-bearing.

A GENUINE, NON-MALICIOUS INTERNAL DISAGREEMENT: IS BEING POTENTIALLY WATCHED COMFORTING OR VIOLATING?
Follows directly from the above. Not everyone would find "you might always be seen from an angle you can't
detect" comforting — some adherents (or a genuine heretical minority) might find the same premise deeply
uncomfortable, even invasive, without either side being wrong about the underlying physics. A real,
textured, non-malicious internal disagreement (fits the project's own non-malice rule) that doesn't require
inventing a villain — just two sincere, differing emotional responses to the same real premise. Good texture
for NPC dialogue/flavor even if never a major plot point.

ZERO AS A MEDITATION OBJECT
Given zero dimensions are framed as "the seed from which geometry grows," not empty absence (E5) — a
genuinely minimal ritual practice: meditating on, or physically marking, a single unmarked point (a dot, a
mark too small to have any extent) as a devotional return-to-origin. Very cheap, very visual, very easy to
depict in-game (a small shrine or personal object that is, deliberately, almost nothing to look at) — pairs
naturally with the "ornament falls away toward the center" architecture idea already in Extrapolation 8.

DIVINATION VIA THE FIFTH DIMENSION
C5 (the 5D-as-axis-of-all-possible-timelines premise, grounded in real many-worlds theory) could ground an
actual in-world divinatory practice — consulting or attempting to perceive adjacent timeline-threads of
oneself, rather than predicting a single fixed future the way most divination systems claim to. Could
manifest as a companion's own personal quirk (prophetic dreams reframed as fragmentary glimpses of nearby
threads, not the future) rather than a formal fortune-telling system — softer and more personal than a full
tarot-equivalent mechanic, but the seed for one exists if a full system is ever wanted.

MEMORIAL ARCHITECTURE WITH DELIBERATE NEGATIVE SPACE
If the dead are understood as "complete, just inaccessible" (Extrapolation 1) rather than gone, a grave or
memorial for this religion's adherents might deliberately include an unused, unfilled portion — a physical
acknowledgment of "the part of them we structurally cannot see," rather than trying to represent the whole
person. A specific, visually distinct funerary-architecture idea, worth remembering whenever Tepenia's
existing funerary/memorial conventions (Goth ossuary practice, etc.) get compared against this religion's
own.

A LITERAL PUZZLE-MECHANIC TIE-IN (VERY SPECULATIVE, GAMEPLAY NOT LORE)
Kissing numbers and sphere-packing (D2) are real, rigorously interesting mathematical puzzle domains. If the
"Scholarly/Diagrammatic" practice track (Extrapolation 6) ever needs an actual interactive minigame or puzzle
system in-engine (not just narrative flavor), real sphere-packing/kissing-number puzzles in low dimensions
are a genuine, real-math-grounded source of puzzle design, distinct from generic "ancient runes" religious
puzzle tropes. Flagged as very speculative and gameplay-system-scoped, well outside what a lore-derivation
pass should be deciding — but worth remembering exists as an option.

BECKER/BECKER/SCHWARZ'S "FAILED AT ITS ORIGINAL PURPOSE, REDEEMED FOR SOMETHING GREATER" AS A FOUNDING MYTH
FOR THE RELIGION ITSELF, NOT THE UNIVERSE
Already logged in overflow_2 as an unused source thread. Worth restating here as a genuine idea: this
religion's own FOUNDING teacher/discoverer figure(s) could have a parallel origin story — someone who set
out to solve a completely unrelated, mundane problem (an engineering question, an ordinary scientific
puzzle) and stumbled into the religion's actual central revelation as an unplanned byproduct, the same way
real string theory was invented for the strong nuclear force and only later turned out to be suited for
something far bigger. A "wrong reason, right discovery" founding myth, distinct from a deliberate-quest
origin story.
